WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.720
A Titan II missile lifts from its path. This flight down the South Atlantic target range

00:10.720 --> 00:15.280
makes history. This is the booster that will carry the Gemini space vehicle on the nation's

00:15.280 --> 00:20.680
next manned space flight program. What makes this test stand as a milestone is a camera

00:20.680 --> 00:25.520
that is mounted on the second stage of the booster. It has been designed to record spectacular

00:25.520 --> 00:31.040
close-ups. As the Titan nears the fringe of space, the first stage shuts down. Now watch.

00:31.040 --> 00:36.560
The second stage ignites and with a mighty blast pushes the first stage away in shattered pieces.

00:36.560 --> 00:43.000
This is what an astronaut in the Gemini will see. At 17,000 miles an hour, the second stage leaves

00:43.000 --> 00:49.000
the abandoned first stage far behind as it soars 5,000 miles down range. The curvature of the Earth

00:49.000 --> 00:54.400
is plainly visible. Through the magic of the camera, Earthlings take their first ride into

00:54.400 --> 00:56.400
space.

